WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:09.950
Twice a day, more or less, the whole ocean rises and falls, and in Florida’s shallow water that can be the difference between floating and sitting on the bottom.

2
00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:14.725
Tides are caused mainly by the moon’s gravity, with help from the sun.

3
00:00:14.975 --> 00:00:17.575
And they don’t behave the same everywhere.

4
00:00:17.825 --> 00:00:19.750
Look at the three curves.

5
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:25.375
A semidiurnal tide has two highs and two lows each day, about equal in height.

6
00:00:25.625 --> 00:00:28.100
That’s Florida’s Atlantic coast.

7
00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:33.400
A mixed tide also has two highs and two lows, but noticeably unequal.

8
00:00:33.650 --> 00:00:35.875
That’s much of our Gulf coast.

9
00:00:36.125 --> 00:00:42.000
And a diurnal tide has just one high and one low a day, as in parts of the Panhandle.

10
00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:44.700
One more fact.

11
00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:49.350
The tidal day is about twenty-four hours and fifty minutes long.

12
00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:54.425
So if high water is at eight this morning, about when is it tomorrow morning?

13
00:00:54.675 --> 00:00:56.625
Around eight fifty.

14
00:00:56.875 --> 00:00:59.575
Roughly fifty minutes later each day.
